PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Key facts preserved: n=10, k=5, EJR (existential: some member of each ℓ-cohesive group ≥ℓ reps). Dominant groups unchanged: N'={1,2,3,8,9,10} (size 6, 3-cohesive on {x1,x2,x3}) requires max_{i∈N′} |A_i ∩ W| ≥3; T={4,5,6,7} (size 4, 2-cohesive on {y4,y5,y6}) requires |W ∩ {y4,y5,y6}| ≥2. Thus |W ∩ {x1,x2,x3}| ≥2 in all valid W (else N' cannot be covered even with y1/z3 + z1). 

Round-1 consensus (colleagues 1-6,8,9): explicit EJR witnesses fix attainable interval exactly [2,3]—W={x1,x2,y4,y5,z1} (voters 8-10 reach 3 via z1; voters 4-5 reach 2) gives voter 1 exactly 2; W={x1,x2,x3,y4,y5} gives exactly 3. All attempts at 4 displace a required y4-6 seat, violating T; attempts at ≤1 force |W ∩ {x1,x2,x3}| ≤1, violating N'. 

Persistent disagreement (7,10): still claim A via {x1,x2,y1,z3,y4} etc.; refuted as size/EJR miscounts (fails to keep both groups covered simultaneously inside |W|=5). No new evidence alters prior conclusion that H is correct.}

